-- boot.lua — the first program the OS runs.
--
-- Kept intentionally tiny: it starts the shell (os.lua) in the
-- foreground, so boot.lua is paused underneath it. A launch returns
-- immediately while the child runs on top, so nothing may follow the
-- Launch() call except the next tick — that tick only happens once the
-- shell has exited, and the OS then has nothing left to run.
--
-- If you want a different startup program, either replace os.lua or
-- edit the Launch() call below.
